WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.675
Now the onboarding itself.

2
00:00:01.675 --> 00:00:06.290
The role-based playbook works one wave
at a time: a single canary server,

3
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.587
then five percent, then a quarter,
and it stops at the first failure.

4
00:00:10.587 --> 00:00:13.513
Each server is checked again
before anything happens.

5
00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.350
Without an explicit confirmation
flag, it never calls the role;

6
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:22.000
it just prints what each server would get,
which is the dry run the role can't do.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.697
With confirmation, it calls
Microsoft's role unchanged,

8
00:00:25.697 --> 00:00:30.438
with the database's values and no stored
secret, and writes a result file.

9
00:00:30.438 --> 00:00:33.980
The older step-by-step playbook
stays for Azure Government.
